DECIDES:

REGIONAL REGULATION CONCERNING THE IMPLEMENTATION OF PROTECTION FOR WOMEN AND CHILDREN VICTIMS OF VIOLENCE.

Article 13

Every victim has the right to receive:

a. protection;
b. information;
c. optimal service;
d. continuous treatment up to the rehabilitation stage; I
e. confidential treatment;
f. psychological and legal assistance; and g. guarantees for rights related to the victim's status as a family member and member of society.

Article 16

(1) The Regional Government establishes an Integrated Service Center (PPT) as the Institution for Organizing, Prevention and Protection of Women and Child Victims of Violence in the region.

(2) PPT as referred to in paragraph (1) consists of elements:

a. health;
b. psychologist;
c. law enforcement;
d. social and empowerment;
e. education and religious affairs;
f. non-governmental organizations; and
g. private sector.
(3) Further provisions regarding PPT as referred to in paragraph (1) are regulated by Regent Regulation.

Article 14

In addition to the rights as referred to in Article 13, child victims of violence also receive special rights including:

a. the right to respect for survival, growth and development;
b. the right to basic services; 1
c. the right to equal protection;
d. the right to be free from various stigmas; and/or e. the right to obtain freedom;
f. the right of victims and families to obtain facilities in the judicial process.

6.13.text:
Article 4

The implementation of protection for women and children from acts of violence aims to: a. prevent all forms of violence including trafficking in persons;

b. eliminate all forms of violence and exploitation against women and children;

c. protect and provide a sense of security for victims of violence;

d. provide services to victims of violence and; e. carry out comprehensive recovery for victims.

Article 13

Every victim has the right to receive:

a. protection;
b. information;
c. optimal service;
d. continuous treatment up to the rehabilitation stage; I
e. confidential treatment;
f. psychological and legal assistance; and g. guarantees for rights related to the victim's status as a family member and member of society.

Article 23

( 1) The community participates in the implementation of protection for victims.

(2) Community participation as referred to in paragraph (1) is in the form of:

a. forming family partners at the village/sub-district level by the community;
b. forming women and children protection units within community organizations;
c. conducting independent socialization of women and children's rights;
d. providing first aid to victims; and
e. reporting to the competent authorities if violence against victims occurs in their environment.
(3) Community participation as referred to in paragraph (1) is carried out by individuals, social community institutions, non-governmental organizations, educational institutions, religious institutions, private sector, and mass media.

Article 16

(1) The Regional Government establishes an Integrated Service Center (PPT) as the Institution for Organizing, Prevention and Protection of Women and Child Victims of Violence in the region.

(2) PPT as referred to in paragraph (1) consists of elements:

a. health;
b. psychologist;
c. law enforcement;
d. social and empowerment;
e. education and religious affairs;
f. non-governmental organizations; and
g. private sector.
(3) Further provisions regarding PPT as referred to in paragraph (1) are regulated by Regent Regulation.

CHAPTER VI

DUTIES AND OBLIGATIONS OF REGIONAL GOVERNMENT Article 15

(1) The Regional Government has the duty to carry out prevention, handling and recovery efforts for victims of violence against Women and Children, by:

a. collecting data and information about Women and Child Victims of Violence;
b. conducting socialization of laws and regulations related to the protection of Women and Child Victims of Violence;
c. providing education on anti-violence values toward children and women; and d. conducting monitoring and evaluation of the implementation of protection for Women and Child victims of violence.
(2) The Regional Government is obliged to carry out prevention, handling and recovery efforts for victims of violence against Women and Children, provide and organize services for victims in the form of:
a. providing and facilitating the formation of integrated services for victims by involving institutions and community elements;
b. encouraging public awareness about the importance of protection for victims; and c. empowering communities to prevent acts of violence.

